  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name='EV Industry: From Data to Decisions' type='storyboard'>
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98142' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='929'>
            <zone h='4878' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99034' x='483' y='929' />
            <zone h='11731' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99034' x='483' y='5807' />
            <zone h='81533' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99034' x='483' y='17538'>
              <flipboard active-id='6' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='The EV Industry at a Glance&#10;&#10;The electric vehicle market is shaped by differences in vehicle categories, driving range, battery technology, and customer ratings. This analysis compares these dimensions to identify patterns that can support product planning and market strategy. The results describe the available dataset and should not be treated as verified global market statistics without further validation.' captured-sheet='EV Market Intelligence' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='Which Vehicle Categories Lead?&#10;&#10;The recorded sales values vary considerably across vehicle categories. This comparison helps identify categories with the largest recorded sales totals and provides a starting point for product-portfolio planning. These figures should be validated against the source data before being interpreted as actual market-wide sales.' captured-sheet='EV Sales by Vehicle Category' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='Driving Range Differs by Vehicle Category&#10;&#10;The dataset shows differences in average driving range across vehicle categories. Luxury sedans and luxury SUVs rank highly in the current comparison. Manufacturers can use this information to evaluate range positioning, while also considering vehicle price, efficiency, and intended use.' captured-sheet='Average Range by Category' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='The Battery Technology Landscape&#10;&#10;NMC and LFP account for the largest numbers of distinct vehicle IDs in this dataset. This indicates that these technologies are well represented in the available records. Vehicle counts alone do not establish global market share or determine which battery technology performs best.' captured-sheet='Battery Technology Distribution' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Customer Ratings Across Manufacturers&#10;&#10;The selected manufacturers have average customer ratings clustered around 4.1. The small differences suggest that ratings alone may not clearly distinguish the leaders. Further analysis should consider sample sizes, rating reliability, vehicle pricing, and performance.' captured-sheet='Customer Ratings by Manufacturer' id='5' />
                  <story-point caption='Strategic Recommendations&#10;&#10;The analysis reveals differences in recorded EV sales, driving range, battery technology representation, and customer ratings. Manufacturers should validate sales data, compare driving range alongside price and efficiency, and investigate battery technology trends before making product portfolio decisions. Customer ratings should be assessed alongside sample sizes and data reliability. Additional verified market and environmental data is needed before drawing conclusions about market share, profitability, or sustainability impact.' captured-sheet='EV Market Intelligence' id='6' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{95A62C35-5F2A-4F5A-8B8E-3145A15B85E8}' />
    </dashboard>
